cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PrivateLabBench in research, please cite the software and the exact release/commit used."
title: "PrivateLabBench"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mahato"
    given-names: "Dipesh Tharu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dipeshbabu/private-lab-bench"
url: "https://github.com/dipeshbabu/private-lab-bench"
license: MIT
version: "0.11.0"
keywords:
  - scientific machine learning
  - evaluation
  - private data
  - reproducibility
  - privacy auditing
  - benchmarking
abstract: >-
  PrivateLabBench is a local-first evaluation framework for scientific machine
  learning on private or restricted data. It supports prediction-table evaluation,
  task plugins, privacy audits, versioned evaluation receipts, and community
  benchmark packs without requiring private-data upload.
